# Architecture — custom store and the golden path

## Context

State lives in a small in-house store: `createStore()` in `app/src/store.ts`
returns `{ getState, dispatch, subscribe }`. It is deliberately NOT
Redux/Zustand/MobX/Jotai. The domain grows through the `Action` discriminated
union in `app/src/types.ts` and the pure reducer in `app/src/reducer.ts` —
see `materials/architecture-brief.md`.

## Rule

- State changes ONLY through `store.dispatch(action)`. NEVER mutate state
  objects in place (`state.tasks.push(...)`, `task.done = true`).
- To add behavior, follow the golden path in this order: add an `Action`
  variant to the union in `app/src/types.ts` → handle it in the `switch` in
  `app/src/reducer.ts` → add an action creator in `app/src/actions.ts` → add
  a colocated `*.test.ts` covering the new reducer case.
- Read state through the selectors in `app/src/selectors.ts` (`visibleTasks`,
  `remainingCount`). DO NOT filter or inspect `state.tasks` inline in
  consumers — add a selector instead.
- NEVER suggest, install, or migrate to Redux, Redux Toolkit, Zustand, MobX,
  Jotai, or any other state library. The custom store IS the architecture.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rE "from ['\"](redux|@reduxjs|zustand|mobx|jotai)" app/src` → zero matches.
2. `grep -rnE "state\.tasks\.(push|pop|splice|sort)\(|\btask\.done\s*=[^=]|\btask\.title\s*=[^=]" app/src` → zero matches (immutable updates only).
3. Every `type: "..."` variant in the `Action` union in `app/src/types.ts` has a matching `case` in `app/src/reducer.ts` and a creator in `app/src/actions.ts`.
4. `cd app && npm test` → all vitest suites green.
